  "current_ecological_hypothesis": "Rain acts as a temporal activation gate on a recurrent, species-specific local chorus template. The most distinctive community-level consequence is not creation of many novel taxa or unusual placement of a fixed number of occupied sites, but deep spatial activation: once a previously silent species is recruited, it disproportionately extends to third and later stops, usually with overlapping/full chorus intensity. The proximal cue and the origin of regional heterogeneity remain unresolved."
